{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dualGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Multigraphs\/documentation\/Multigraphs\/Pseudograph","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Multigraphs11PseudographV","text":"Pseudograph","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A pseudograph on ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<faceCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with one edge per edge of the graph.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"type":"text","text":" is the face at position "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"faces"},{"type":"text","text":". The edge at position "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":" is the dual of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":"th edge of the graph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":": it joins the face to the right of that edge crossed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from its end with the lower vertex number (for a self-loop, its end listed first) and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"face to its right crossed from the other end, in that order. A bridge has one face on both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sides, so its dual is a self-loop; the edges around a vertex of degree d become d edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"around its dual face, parallel when two of them separate the same two faces. Faces are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counted per connected component, so the dual of a disconnected graph is the disjoint union"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its components’ duals, and an isolated vertex contributes nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n + m)."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"dualGraph()","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dualGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Pseudograph","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Multigraphs11PseudographV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"modules":[{"name":"Planarity"}],"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:9Planarity15PlanarEmbeddingV9dualGraph11Multigraphs11PseudographVySiGyF","symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"Planarity","remoteSource":{"fileName":"DualGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Planarity\/DualGraph.swift#L20"}},"abstract":[{"text":"The dual graph of the embedding: a vertex for each face, and for each edge an edge joining","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the two faces it separates.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding"]]},"variants":[{"paths":